Hi Neal:

Attached find a "DLL" and a function that can compute the "Ei(x)" 
function.  You need to first load the DLL using:

dyn.load("ei.dll")

then use the function, e.g.

> Ei(0.5)
[1] 0.4542199

The function is simple - given below:

Ei <- function(x) {
val <- .Fortran("eix",x,ei=0.)$ei
val
}

The DLL was created using "mingw" g77 compiler and it works in R on 
Windows.  I am not sure whether this would work in Splus, I think it 
should. 

Best,
Ravi.

