Message-ID: <E09E527B56BE2D438A3D6A246DDD27A9165777@roper-cv.qld.cmis.CSIRO.AU>

The 
optimal correlation is achieved by giving the levels of the factor variable the 
class means for the other variable.  A simple function to do what you want 
would be:

 

cor.xf <- function(x, f) {

    m <- tapply(x, f, 
mean)

    cor(x, m[f])

}

 

Enjoy.

 

V.

