4. Response
I haven't read the reference you cited but I hope they added that all of these
stepwise
procedures can be disasters in terms of overfitting, non-preservation of
confidence interval
coverage and type I error, biased estimates of regression coefficients,
inflated R^2, inflated
adjusted R^2, etc., etc.  See more at http://www.pitt.edu/~wpilib/statfaq.html
and
http://hesweb1.med.virginia.edu/biostat/rms .
