From jpnolan at american.edu  Mon Jan 13 16:31:40 2003
From: jpnolan at american.edu (John Nolan)
Date: Mon, 13 Jan 2003 11:31:40 -0500
Subject: package to produce webpages with embedded graphs
Message-ID: <OF4CCDC6FA.5474246A-ON85256CAD.005ACA2E-85256CAD.005ACA3C@american.edu>

htmlMaker is a simple package to allow one to produce webpages 
with graphs in R or S-Plus.  The program generates the html 
commands to start a page, produces graphics in png format, 
includes graphs in the webpage, and closes the file.  Three 
types of plot (x-y points, barplot and boxplot) can be "active", 
i.e. putting the cursor over the point shows the coordinates and
clicking on the point will follow a link.
The result is less interactive than an S-Plus "graphlet" or a java application,
but it is simple (pure html output, so it can be viewed by anyone
with a browser) and can be run under R in interactive or batch mode.
The code is available at http://academic2.american.edu/~jpnolan, 
follow the link "Producing web pages with graphs from R or S-Plus".

