Subject: Multivariate Kernel Densities
Message-ID: <5.2.0.9.2.20030115171945.019bc760@129.15.69.4>

Dear List,

I know that there are 2-D kernel density estimators available, for example 
within MASS, but are there kernel density estimators available for 
dimensions greater than 3?  I realize that the required sample size 
increases dramatically with dimensionality, so I probably wouldn't be able 
to use anything with dimensions greater than 5 or 6, possibly 7.

As an aside (and admittedly off topic) how should I deal with correlated 
dimensions?  As a simple example, in a two-dimensional density a ridge (or 
valley) in the surface could be caused by a correlation, though a bump 
wouldn't be. Is this best handled by "good judgement," or should I 
seriously consider recasting correlated dimensions into an orthogonal eigen 
space?  Or, is it so much harder than I realize that perhaps I'm best 
advised to avoid the problem altogether?

Thanks for your insights.

Kim Elmore
