> 
> 10,000 observations for a 1D log-normal is data-rich:  10,000 observations
> for a multimodal density in 3D is a completely different matter. You can't
> even begin to count normals, as in kD they have lots of parameters each,
> and you have to be able to fit the mixture of normals somehow.  By MLE, it
> is a high-dimensional optimization problem with many local maxima, hard
